        "params": {
          "text": "**SP01 \u2014 Build a square wave from smooth tones**  \n**Do more harmonics remove the ringing near a jump?** Run **2 s at 128 Hz**; open Scope.  \nAt state time 0.125 s: one 1.27324 V; three 1.10347 V; five 1.06305 V. At jumps every partial sum is 0.  \nChange weight9 factor to 0. Which 18 Hz component disappears? Scope: inspect 0\u20130.5 s; see guide for Spectrum settings.  \n[Open SP01 student lab](qrc:/s7studio/help/education/labs/SP01-fourier-synthesis/README.md) \u00b7 [MIT teaching materials](https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/6-003-signals-and-systems-fall-2011/resources/mit6_003f11_lec15/) \u00b7 [S7 signal sources](qrc:/s7studio/help/docs/SIGNAL_SOURCES.md)",
          "text_format": "markdown",
          "width": 1562,
          "height": 260,
          "font_size": 18
        }
      }
